      "quote_check": "ok",
      "unit": "percent",
      "kind": "change",
      "passage": "Gross slippage ratio at 2.11% is down by 102 basis points QOQ. Our net slippage ratio at 1.05% is down 128 basis points QOQ. Our retail asset quality is stabilizing. \u2022 Retail business net slippages and net credit costs are lower than what we reported in Q2 FY25. \u2022 Net credit cost is 0.73%, down 65 basis points QOQ. Our domestic subsidiaries delivered steady performance: H1FY26 total profit at Rs. 936 crores with a return on investment in domestic subsidiaries of 49%. \u2022 Axis Finance: o H1 PAT grew 18% YOY to Rs. 385 crores. o Asset quality metrics remained stable with net NPA at 0.42%. \u2022 Axis AMC: o H1FY26 PAT grew 11% YOY to Rs. 271 crores. \u2022 Axis Securities: o Customer base grew 15% YOY and the H1FY26 PAT stood at Rs. 175 crores. \u2022 Axis Capital: o H1FY26 PAT stood at Rs. 93 crores.",
